tioned in the resume or cover letter; the experience seems more focused on administrative, production planning, and general business development support within a local context.\",\"The listed \'Responsibilities\' for \'Administrative Executive\' and \'Officer-Planning\' are administrative, production-focused, or related to software/RPL processes, not directly to sales pipeline management, closing deals, or client acquisition.\",\"While the applicant mentions \'customer communication\' and \'client service management\', specific sales achievements or quotas are not provided.\",\"The roles do not clearly demonstrate experience with \'multilingual\' skills or strong \'cultural awareness\' as desired attributes.\",\"The provided portfolio link leads to a Google Drive folder with certificates and academic project documents, not a traditional sales portfolio showcasing deals, client successes, or sales-related projects.\",\"The requested salary of $150-$300/month is very low for an International Sales Executive role, potentially indicating a mismatch in expectations or a misunderstanding of the position\'s scope/value in some markets.\"]','The applicant demonstrates general administrative and some business development support experience, along with claimed sales-related skills in the cover letter. However, direct evidence of international B2B sales experience, a core requirement, is missing. Their stated experience is not clearly aligned with the specific responsibilities of an International Sales Executive. Further investigation into their actual sales track record, particularly international and B2B, would be necessary. The extr','{\"other\": [], \"emails\": [\"shamimaasha74@gmail.com\", \"headswe@daffodilvarsity.edu.bd\", \"kaushik.swe@daffodilvarsity.edu.bd\"], \"github\": [], \"phones\": [\"01977790237\", \"+88 019 7779 0237\", \"+880 1847140016\", \"+880 01847140142\"], \"linkedin\": [\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shamima-islam-969846171/\"], \"portfolio\": [\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1FzQNaA17NZ12OH8q0tXirz0JNMqF-Fso?usp=sharing\"]}','[\"Candidate explicitly states experience in telesales, lead generation, and relationship management, directly aligning with sales requirements.\",\"Claims confidence in identifying business opportunities, building client relationships, and contributing to revenue growth.\",\"Resume indicates 4 years of work experience, which meets the job\'s requirement of \'3+ years experience\'.\",\"The applicant\'s current role as \'Administrative Executive\' and past roles as \'Officer-Planning\' and \'Admin Executive - Business Development\' suggest exposure to administrative and potentially coordination tasks that could support sales.\",\"Experience in \'Digital Marketing\' and \'Content Writing\' could be beneficial for lead generation in a sales role.\",\"The cover letter expresses motivation and a results-driven attitude.\"]'),('67ad3cc2-ed93-4c6d-b640-ef5b28a2c8d4','f24794fa-3869-4b31-b0b8-612e3bf9f09c','full-stack-developer','Full Stack Developer','Razi Ullah','iamraziullah07@gmail.com','+92 3664610578','Pakistan','Associate Fullstack Engineer@TechClan',1,'Market Competitive','https://www.linkedin.com/in/raziullah/','https://dev.dailyfit.egenesisai.cloud','public/full-stack-developer/1779291484969-23x092.pdf','Dear Hiring Team,\n\nI am Razi Ullah, a full-stack software engineer with experience across React/Next.js, TypeScript, Node.js/NestJS, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Prisma, CI/CD, and production integrations. I am interested in this role because it closely aligns with the stack I currently work with and the type of product-focused engineering I enjoy.\n\nIn my current role as an Associate Software Engineer at TechClan, I work on production React-based applications serving 100k+ users. My work includes shipping full-stack features and bug fixes, working with Temporal workflows, integrating Hubstaff timer functionality, implementing Datadog tracing, adding Mixpanel backend events, and handling frontend analytics. I also contribute to YAML CI/CD pipelines, write unit tests, review pull requests, resolve merge conflicts, debug production issues, and collaborate closely with product and design teams.\n\nBeyond my professional role, I built DailyFit, a multi-tenant gym management SaaS using Next.js 15, TypeScript, Prisma, PostgreSQL, NextAuth, and Docker. This gave me deeper hands-on experience with tenant-scoped data access, onboarding flows, product thinking, and deployment.\n\nAlthough my formal professional experience is around one year, it has been production-heavy and closely aligned with the expectations of this role. I care about clean, typed, tested code, fast iteration, and owning features from idea to release. I would be excited to bring this mindset and technical experience to your React + Node/Postgres stack.\n\nSincerely,  \nRazi Ullah','career-page','rejected',NULL,'{}',NULL,'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36','2026-05-20 15:38:06','2026-05-22 09:01:06',77,'high','[\"full-stack\",\"typescript\",\"react\",\"node\",\"postgres\",\"cloud\",\"mindset\",\"full\",\"stack\",\"technical\",\"code\",\"features\"]','[\"supabase\",\"comfort\",\"developer\"]','Matched 12/15 keywords for \"Full Stack Developer\". Required ~3y, candidate has 1y. Despite falling short on the 3+ years of experience requirement, the candidate demonstrates an impressively strong technical skill set, direct experience with the specific technologies listed in the job description (React, Node, Postgres/Supabase, TypeScript, CI/CD), and a clear product mindset. Their projects and current role show a high level of responsibility and impact for their experience level. The candidate\'s self-developed SaaS platform (DailyFit) is a significant highlight, illustrating end-to-end feature ownership and a solid understanding of software architecture and deployment. Given the strong alignment in tech stack and demonstrated c