buting to best practices.\"]'),('7a1516e4-9d6c-4d71-8687-6390c49768d7','f24794fa-3869-4b31-b0b8-612e3bf9f09c','full-stack-developer','Full Stack Developer','Hamza Sarwar','Engr.hamzarao@gmail.com','+923032912247','Pakistan','Full stack development',2,'Negotiable','https://www.linkedin.com/in/hamzasarwar-full-stack-developer?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_android',NULL,'public/full-stack-developer/1779268094882-gguvcx.pdf','Dear Hiring Manager,\n\nI’m excited to apply for the Full Stack Developer role. While my resume reflects two years of formal experience, the reality is that I’ve been building, breaking, and fixing software for much longer.\n\nI started coding around seven years ago, long before I had a professional title attached to it. That journey included rebuilding a hacked e commerce site for a family friend, learning hard lessons from failed late night deployments, and helping teammates solve problems when deadlines were tight and stress was high. Those experiences may not appear on a timesheet, but they shaped the way I approach development and teamwork.\n\nOver time, I’ve worked on shipping features, debugging memory leaks, improving slow SQL queries that affected live systems, and collaborating closely with QA to make sure products work smoothly for real users. I’ve learned that good software is not just about writing code. It is about problem solving, communication, ownership, and staying calm when things go wrong.\n\nThat mindset is what I bring to every project and every team I work with. I’m always willing to learn, adapt, and put in the effort needed to deliver meaningful results.\n\nI would love the opportunity to contribute my skills and experience to your team. Thank you for your time and consideration.\n\nWarm regards,\nHamza Sarwar','career-page','reviewing',NULL,'{}',NULL,'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 10; K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Mobile Safari/537.36','2026-05-20 09:08:18','2026-05-2