ation, high-quality research, and engaging delivery for an Australian client.\",\"Strategized digital content delivery and optimized business workflows, ensuring high-quality engagement and measurable growth.\"]'),('e46dc7ac-d765-4145-b0d0-ba6f0f55dbcd','f24794fa-3869-4b31-b0b8-612e3bf9f09c','full-stack-developer','Full Stack Developer','Muhammad Jahad Tariq','muhammadjahadt@gmail.com','+923270977690','Pakistan','Frontend Developer @ Nazadv',4,'negotiable','https://www.linkedin.com/in/muhammad-jahad-tariq-75aa652b4/','https://www.linkedin.com/in/muhammad-jahad-tariq-75aa652b4/','public/full-stack-developer/1779250069974-egpxvi.docx','Muhammad Jahad Tariq\nmuhammadjahadt@gmail.com · +92-327-0977-690\nlinkedin.com/in/muhammad-jahad-tariq-75aa652b4\n\nMay 20, 2026\n\nI build features across the full stack, ship them to production, and take responsibility for what happens after. That\'s exactly what this role is asking for — so let me be direct about the match.\n\nOver the past five years I\'ve worked end-to-end on production systems serving real users at scale: React and Next.js frontends, Node.js backends with REST APIs and Postgres-compatible databases, CI/CD pipelines, and TypeScript throughout. At NAZ-ADV I owned a complete onboarding flow redesign that moved conversion by 4%, cut page load times by 15%, and shipped via a Jenkins pipeline I built myself — reducing deployment time by 40%. At Billmode I reduced API response time by 18% and database retrieval time by 25% through targeted backend and query optimization on a live SaaS product.\n\nI\'ve collaborated daily with product and design, contributed to architecture decisions, and written the kind of code that gets reviewed, merged, and maintained — not just shipped and forgotten. I\'m comfortable designing database schemas, writing tests, and working on Edge backends. Supabase is on my radar and something I can move fast on.\n\nStack: React · Next.js · Node.js · TypeScript · REST APIs · MongoDB · MySQL · Postgres · CI/CD · AWS · GCP · 5+ years full-stack\n\nYou have three open spots. I\'d be a strong fit for any of them, and I\'m ready to prove it in a technical screen. Happy to share code, walk through past architecture decisions, or jump on a call this week.\n\nWith respect,\nMuhammad Jahad Tariq','career-page','rejected',NULL,'{}',NULL,'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36','2026-05-20 04:07:51','2026-05-21 16:58:38',35,'low','[\"full-stack\",\"typescript\",\"react\",\"node\",\"postgres\",\"supabase\",\"comfort\",\"full\",\"stack\",\"developer\",\"technical\",\"code\",\"features\"]','[\"cloud\",\"mindset\"]','Matched 13/15 keywords for \"Full Stack Developer\". Required ~3y, candidate has 4y. Muhammad Jahad Tariq is a strong candidate for the Full Stack Developer role. His extensive experience with the required technologies (React, Node, Postgres, TypeScript), comfort with CI/CD and cloud, and demonstrated product mindset align very well with the job requirements. He has successfully delivered significant improvements in past roles and clearly articulates his fit for an end-to-end development position. The unparseable resume is a minor concern, but the cover letter provides sufficient detail to assess his qualifications.','2026-05-20 04:08:00',11442,'[\"TypeScript\",\"React\",\"Node.js\",\"Postgres\",\"Next.js\",\"REST APIs\",\"CI/CD\",\"MongoDB\",\"MySQL\",\"AWS\",\"GCP\",\"Jenkins\",\"Supabase\"]','[\"Full Stack Developer\",\"Frontend Developer\"]',5.000000,'Not provided','[\"Resume / CV text was unparseable, relying solely on provided form fields and cover letter.\"]','Muhammad Jahad Tariq is a strong candidate for the Full Stack Developer role. His extensive experience with the required technologies (React, Node, Postgres, TypeScript), comfort with CI/CD and cloud, and demonstrated product mindset align very well with the job requirements. He has successfully delivered significant improvements in past roles and clearly articulates his fit for an end-to-end development position. The unparseable resume is a minor concern, but the cover letter provides sufficien','{\"other\": [], \"emails\": [\"muhammadjahadt@gmail.com\"], \"github\": [], \"phones\": [\"+923270977690\", \"+92-327-0977-690\"], \"linkedin\": [\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/muhammad-jahad-tariq-75aa652b4/\"], \"portfolio\": [\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/muhammad-jahad-tariq-75aa652b4/\"]}','[\"Over 5 years of full-stack experience, exceeding the 3+ years requirement.\",\"Proficient in React, Node.js, and Postgres, directly aligning with the job description\'s tech stack.\",\"Experience with CI/CD pipelines (Jenkins) and cloud platforms (AWS, GCP), demonstrating comfort with CI/CD and cloud.\",\"Strong product mindset evidenced by contributions to improved conversion rates, reduced page load times, and optimized API response/database retrieval times.\",\"Experience with end-to-end feature development and shipping production code.\",\"Directly addresses key requirements such as collaboration with PM and design, participation in code reviews and technical decisions.\",\"Has experience designing database schemas and writing tests.\",\"Familiarity with Supabase, indicating adaptability and willingness to learn specified technologies.\"]'),('e62e38ca-1a13-46d0-bc68-95322bd47489','f24794fa-3869-4b31-b0b8-612e3bf9f09c','full-stack-developer','Full Stack Developer','Ahmad Arif','ahmadarifdev786@gmail.com','+923006830864','Pakistan','Fullstack engineer',6,'Negotiable','https://www.linkedin.com/in/ahmad-arif-ba6862218/','https://ahmad.websol.space/','public/full-stack-developer/1780981152578-isndzq.pdf','Hi,\n\nIf you\'re serious about finding a reliable and skilled developer, I\'m equally serious about my profession and the quality of work I deliver.\n\nWith over 6 years of experience in software development, specializing in React.js and Next.js, I focus on building scalable, high-performance applicati